From 5f0f6c7783cf47e953261d3f3503fb786f20bf88 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matthew Schwartz <matthew.schwartz@linux.dev>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 23:34:27 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] memory: add cgroup_mem from the app's systemd cgroup

Desktops and launchers following systemd's app unit convention run each
app in its own app-*.scope or app-*.service under app.slice. A launcher
can do the same per game, so the unit holds the game and any helper
processes it starts.

Add a CGROUP row showing anon + shmem from the memory.stat of the cgroup
the app runs in, when that cgroup is inside such a unit. It covers
everything in the cgroup, so a launcher that shares the app's unit is
included. It leaves out page cache, and counts GPU buffers only on
drivers that charge them to the cgroup as shmem (msm, i915 iGPU,
panfrost/panthor, v3d), not TTM ones (amdgpu, xe, nouveau).

Services under app.slice outside the convention are skipped. procmem
and the process_rss log column are unchanged. Off in preset 4 like
procmem.
